cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Condensate Theorem: Sparse Attention Without Approximation"
authors:
  - family-names: "Granados"
    given-names: "Jorge"
type: "article"
date-released: 2026-01-31
repository-code: "https://github.com/JorgeLRW/condensate-theorem"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "attention mechanism"
  - "sparse attention"
  - "transformer"
  - "efficient inference"
  - "condensate theorem"
abstract: |
  We prove that trained transformer models concentrate >99% of attention mass
  on a sparse, predictable manifold C_i = {Anchor} ∪ {Window} ∪ {Top-K}.
  This enables exact O(n) attention computation with 157x measured speedup,
  scaling to 1,257x at 1M tokens.
